4-.26l.004-.002c.314-.106.892-.178 1.554-.178.663 0 1.241.071 1.554.178l.005.002a1.025 1.025 0 0 1 .405.26c.478.472 1.537 2.895 2.549 5.887.886 2.617 1.479 4.91 1.552 5.89.002.032.005.066.005.098a.76.76 0 0 1-.491.713z"></path></svg>Aircall</li><li class="logo-strip__more">Your bank</li></ul></div></div></div></div></section><section class="section section--light ab-story" id="trust"><div class="container"><div class="ab-story__grid"><div class="ab-story__lead" data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">Why trust is the whole job</p><blockquote class="ab-quote">For many of your clients, an unexpected call about money isn&#x27;t a reminder. It&#x27;s a reason to be afraid.</blockquote><p class="ab-quote__cite">LexCollect exists to close the gap between what a family has paid and what your firm can see.</p></div><ol class="ab-chapters"><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="0"><span class="ab-chapters__kicker">The client</span><h3>Living with a fear most of us never carry</h3><p>Many of the people your firm represents are undocumented, waiting years on a decision, or part of a mixed-status family. A knock at the door, an official-looking letter or a call from a number they don&#x27;t know can feel like the start of losing everything they&#x27;ve built here.</p></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="100"><span class="ab-chapters__kicker">The payment</span><h3>Every installment is a sacrifice</h3><p>They work long hours, often in jobs with no security, to keep a household running here and often a family back home. Your fee is paid out of that, month after month, sometimes by a brother, a spouse or an employer. Each payment says: I trust you with my future.</p></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="200"><span class="ab-chapters__kicker">The break</span><h3>When the firm can&#x27;t see it, trust breaks</h3><p>When a payment lands in one system and not another, the firm asks about money the family already paid, or says nothing while they quietly fall behind. Either way the client hears the same thing: they don&#x27;t see me. Clients who stop trusting the firm stop answering, and a case that depends on staying in touch is put at risk.</p></li></ol></div></div></section><section class="hm-proof" aria-label="Results from the first deployment"><div class="container"><p class="hm-proof__intro" data-reveal="true">From the first deployment, inside a high-volume immigration firm. <a href="<?php echo esc_url( lexcollect_page_url( 'results' ) ); ?>">Read the results <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p><ul class="hm-proof__grid"><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="0"><span class="hm-proof__num" data-count="21.4" data-decimals="1" data-prefix="$" data-suffix="M">$21.4M</span><span class="hm-proof__label">receivables book reconciled to the firm&#x27;s own ground truth</span></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="80"><span class="hm-proof__num" data-count="3.5" data-decimals="1" data-prefix="$" data-suffix="M">$3.5M</span><span class="hm-proof__label">in balances re-linked to the right clients through a system migration</span></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="160"><span class="hm-proof__num" data-count="228" data-decimals="0" data-prefix="" data-suffix="">228</span><span class="hm-proof__label">clients who wanted to pay, reached with one update-your-card message instead of a collections call</span></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="240"><span class="hm-proof__num" data-count="928" data-decimals="0" data-prefix="$" data-suffix="K">$928K</span><span class="hm-proof__label">kept out of hard debt by separating failed cards from delinquency</span></li></ul></div></section><section class="section section--light hm-recon" id="reconcile"><div class="container"><div class="hm-recon__grid"><div class="hm-recon__copy" data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">One source of truth</p><h2>Most immigration firms have four versions of what a family has paid.</h2><p class="lead">A deposit at the consultation, installments from a sponsor&#x27;s card, a filing fee passed through, a payment taken at the front desk. The case system, the processor, the books and the bank each hold a piece, so the partners pick one and hope. LexCollect ties them into one number and explains every dollar of difference.</p><ul class="hm-ticks"><li>Payments traced from the case system to the bank deposit</li><li>Payments by a relative, sponsor or employer credited to the right client</li><li>Each matter in a household kept apart, so one case never looks overdue for another&#x27;s payment</li><li>A certified snapshot every month, so trends are real history</li></ul></div><div class="hm-recon__panel" data-recon="true" data-state="after" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="hm-recon__head"><span class="hm-recon__title">Collections this month</span><div class="hm-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Show the numbers"><button type="button" data-recon-set="before" aria-pressed="false">Before</button><button type="button" data-recon-set="after" aria-pressed="true">With LexCollect</button></div></div><ul class="hm-recon__rows"><li style="--off:-0.242"><span class="hm-recon__src"><b>Case system</b><span>MyCase</span></span><span class="hm-recon__track"><span class="hm-recon__amt"><span class="v-before">$411,410.00</span><span class="v-after">$412,860.00</span></span></span><span class="hm-recon__note"><span class="v-before is-off">Doesn&#x27;t match</span><span class="v-after">+$1,450.00 · 2 payments made by a relative, now credited to the client</span></span></li><li style="--off:0.000"><span class="hm-recon__src"><b>Processor</b><span>LawPay</span></span><span class="hm-recon__track"><span class="hm-recon__amt"><span class="v-before">$412,860.00</span><span class="v-after">$412,860.00</span></span></span><span class="hm-recon__note"><span class="v-before">Matches</span><span class="v-after">Matches the deposit record</span></span></li><li style="--off:0.200"><span class="hm-recon__src"><b>Books</b><span>QuickBooks</span></span><span class="hm-recon__track"><span class="hm-recon__amt"><span class="v-before">$414,060.00</span><span class="v-after">$412,860.00</span></span></span><span class="hm-recon__note"><span class="v-before is-off">Doesn&#x27;t match</span><span class="v-after">−$1,200.00 · 1 duplicate entry removed</span></span></li><li style="--off:-1.000"><span class="hm-recon__src"><b>Bank</b><span>Operating account</span></span><span class="hm-recon__track"><span class="hm-recon__amt"><span class="v-before">$402,331.06</span><span class="v-after">$412,860.00</span></span></span><span class="hm-recon__note"><span class="v-before is-off">Doesn&#x27;t match</span><span class="v-after">+$10,528.94 · deposit in transit, cleared Oct 1</span></span></li></ul><div class="hm-recon__foot"><span class="v-before">4 systems, 4 different answers</span><span class="v-after">Reconciled <b>$412,860.00</b> · every difference explained</span><span class="hm-example">Example data</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="section hm-explore" id="platform"><div class="container"><div class="hm-explore__head" data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">The platform</p><h2>One place for the whole receivables job.</h2><p class="lead">Four jobs a high-level accounting department does for a firm, each one a working part of LexCollect today.</p></div><div class="hm-tabs" data-tabs="true" data-autoplay="9000" data-reveal="true"><div class="hm-tabs__list" aria-label="Platform capabilities"><button type="button" class="hm-tab is-active" data-tab="see" id="tab-see" aria-controls="panel-see"><span class="hm-tab__num">01</span><span class="hm-tab__label">See every dollar</span></button><button type="button" class="hm-tab" data-tab="connect" id="tab-connect" aria-controls="panel-connect"><span class="hm-tab__num">02</span><span class="hm-tab__label">Reach families with care</span></button><button type="button" class="hm-tab" data-tab="recover" id="tab-recover" aria-controls="panel-recover"><span class="hm-tab__num">03</span><span class="hm-tab__label">Recover hard debt</span></button><button type="button" class="hm-tab" data-tab="run" id="tab-run" aria-controls="panel-run"><span class="hm-tab__num">04</span><span class="hm-tab__label">Run like a department</span></button></div><div class="hm-panel is-active" data-panel="see" id="panel-see" aria-labelledby="tab-see"><div class="hm-panel__copy"><h3>A receivables number the partners can trust, every month.</h3><p>One live view across your case system, processor, books and bank, with a certified snapshot on the 1st that you can hand to the partners.</p><ul class="hm-ticks"><li>Aging and open AR from real history, not a re-run of today</li><li>Expected deposits by week</li><li>Unmatched payments counted and queued, never parked</li></ul><p class="hm-panel__screens"><span>Screens</span> AR Management · Controller view · AR Movement · Monthly snapshots</p></div><div class="hm-panel__visual"><div class="hm-mock"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Open receivables · certified on the 1st</span><span class="hm-example">Example data</span></div><svg class="hm-chart" viewBox="0 0 440 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="ar-chart-t"><title id="ar-chart-t">Open receivables by month, certified on the 1st. Example data, falling from $2.71M in April to $2.49M in September.</title><line class="hm-chart__grid" x1="20" x2="420" y1="124" y2="124"></line><line class="hm-chart__grid" x1="20" x2="420" y1="76" y2="76"></line><line class="hm-chart__grid" x1="20" x2="420" y1="28" y2="28"></line><line class="hm-chart__base" x1="20" x2="420" y1="172" y2="172"></line><g class="hm-chart__bar is-labelled"><title>Apr: $2.71M</title><rect class="hm-chart__hit" x="4" y="8" width="72" height="184"></rect><path d="M20,172 V45.920000000000016 q0,-4 4,-4 h32 q4,0 4,4 V172 Z"></path><text class="hm-chart__val" x="40" y="33.920000000000016" text-anchor="middle">$2.71M</text><text class="hm-chart__tick" x="40" y="1