n>−8.1% in six months</span></div></div></div></div><div class="hm-panel" data-panel="connect" id="panel-connect" aria-labelledby="tab-connect"><div class="hm-panel__copy"><h3>Most late accounts aren&#x27;t refusals. They&#x27;re families the firm lost touch with.</h3><p>A clear, respectful message, by email or text, reaches the right client at the right moment, in your firm&#x27;s name and voice. A person steps in only when the family needs one.</p><ul class="hm-ticks"><li>Balances reconciled before anything is sent</li><li>Failed cards get an update link, not a collections call</li><li>Every reply and promise logged to the account</li></ul><p class="hm-panel__screens"><span>Screens</span> Connect queue · Email &amp; SMS · Client lists · Commitments</p></div><div class="hm-panel__visual"><div class="hm-mock hm-mock--thread"><div class="hm-mock__head"><span>Ana Morales · Payment plan</span><span class="hm-example">Example data</span></div><ol class="hm-thread"><li class="hm-msg hm-msg--out"><span class="hm-msg__meta">Text · 9:14 AM · Delivered</span>Hi Ana, it&#x27;s Lucía from the billing team at Morgan &amp; Hale. Thank you for staying with your plan. This month&#x27;s card payment didn&#x27;t go through. Nothing about your case has changed. You can update the card here in about a minute: <u>pay.morganhale.com/u/8F2K</u></li><li class="hm-msg hm-msg--in"><span class="hm-msg__meta">Reply · 9:31 AM</span>Done, thank you for telling me. Can I catch up on the 15th?</li><li class="hm-event"><i class="hm-dot hm-dot--ok" aria-hidden="true"></i> Card updated · promise logged: $1,050 on Oct 15</li></ol></div></div></div><div class="hm-panel" data-panel="recover" id="panel-recover" aria-labelledby="tab-recover"><div class="hm-panel__copy"><h3>Older balances get a plan the family can keep.</h3><p>Ninety-day-plus accounts get patience with a structure: a reconciled balance first, a clear and respectful message, a plan that fits a paycheck, and a record of every promise.</p><u