h-volume immigration firm running MyCase, Filevine, LawPay, HubSpot and QuickBooks, with thousands of payment plans and families paying for one another.</p><a class="hm-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( lexcollect_page_url( 'results' ) ); ?>">Read the full results <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><ul class="hm-findings"><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="0"><span class="hm-findings__num">$928K</span><p>across 228 clients whose cards had failed. They got an update-your-card message, not a collections call.</p></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="90"><span class="hm-findings__num">428</span><p>contracts marked Paid with about 4% actually collected, found, reclassified and audited.</p></li><li data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="180"><span class="hm-findings__num">561</span><p>orphan contracts re-linked to the right clients, and 89 duplicate client records merged.</p></li></ul></div></div></section><section class="section hm-roles" id="who"><div class="container"><div class="hm-roles__head" data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">Suited to your firm</p><h2>Built for everyone who touches the money, and the relationship.</h2><p class="lead">Roles, queues, messages, case types and integrations are configuration, not code. Your clients hear from your firm, in your voice, never from a stranger.</p></div><ul class="hm-roles__grid"><li class="hm-role" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="0"><span class="hm-role__who">Partners &amp; owners</span><h3>The number, and the reason behind it</h3><p>Certified AR, team performance and the biggest movers in the book this month.</p></li><li class="hm-role" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="70"><span class="hm-role__who">Controllers &amp; administrators</span><h3>Reconciled, forecastable, defensible</h3><p>Expected deposits, cash-flow analytics and the month-end packet, ready.</p></li><li class="hm-role" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="140"><span class="hm-role__who">Billing &amp; client relations</span><h3>A queue that&#x27;s already prioritized</h3><p>Messages, promises, hardship requests and the client&#x27;s full ledger on one screen.</p></li><li class="hm-role" data-reveal="true" data-reveal-delay="210"><span class="hm-role__who">Case teams</span><h3>Attorneys and paralegals see what billing sees</h3><p>The plan, the payments, deadline watch and an inbox for escalations that need someone who knows the client.</p></li></ul></div></section><section class="section section--rule hm-faq" id="faq"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div data-reveal="true"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>What firm owners ask first.</h2></div><div class="faq"><details open=""><summary><h3>What is LexCollect?</h3></summary><div><p>An accounts-receivable accounting service built for immigration and humanitarian law firms: the visibility, automation and client connection of a high-level accounting department, delivered as software and run by people who know receivables. It reconciles your case system, processor, books and bank into one source of truth, then runs the outreach, promises, escalations and reporting on top of it.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>Why does an immigration firm need this more than other firms?</h3></summary><div><p>Because the billing is harder and the relationship is more fragile. Flat fees paid over months or years, payments from relatives and sponsors, several matters in one household, names spelled three different ways, and clients for whom an unexpected call about money can be frightening. Getting the record right is how the firm keeps their trust.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>Is LexCollect a collections agency?</h3></summary><div><p>No. Nobody from LexCollect calls your clients. LexCollect provides the connection: the reconciled book, the queues, the respectful automated email and text, the promises and the record. Your own team handles the conversations that need a person, with the client&#x27;s reconciled ledger in front of them.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>Does it replace our case management or accounting software?</h3></summary><div><p>No. LexCollect sits across the systems you already run and reconciles them. Your team keeps working in the same tools.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>Which systems does it connect to?</h3></summary><div><p>Any CRM or practice system that exports or has an API. Working today with MyCase, Filevine, LawPay, HubSpot, QuickBooks, plus bank deposits and spreadsheet exports. If you run something else, tell us on the first call.</p></div></details><details><summary><h3>What does the first call involve?</h3></summary><div><p>One conversation about your practice and your systems, then a first look at your book: what&#x27;s late, which payments were never credited, which families have simply lost touch, and what you could recover first. No exports needed for the first call.</p></div></details></div></div></div></section><section class="section hm-start" id="contact"><div class="container"><div class="hm-start__grid"><div class="hm-start__copy"><p class="eyebrow">Book a call</p><h2>See where money, and trust, are slipping.</h2><p class="lead">Tell us about your practice and the systems you use. We&#x27;ll show you where payments are going unseen, which families have quietly lost touch, and what a respectful message would bring back.</p><ol class="next-steps"><li><b>We reply within one business day</b><span>to set a time that works for your team.</span></li><li><b>We walk through your systems</b><span>Your case management, payment and accounting tools, and where payments seem to go missing.</span></li><li><b>You see what&#x27;s recoverable</b><span>Late, never credited, failed-card and ready-to-reconnect, with a dollar figure on each.</span></li></ol><p class="hm-start__alt">Prefer email? <a href="mailto:jeff@lex-collect.com">jeff@lex-collect.com</a><br/>Already a client? <a href="<?php echo esc_url( LEXCOLLECT_APP_LOGIN_URL )